WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.170
This is Kingda Ka,

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.420
the tallest roller coaster in the world.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.280
At 139 meters, it's nearly the height

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.980
of the Great Pyramid of Giza.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.810
But what if we built a
roller coaster even taller?

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.890
What if there was a
coaster that went as high

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.090
as the tallest building on
Earth, the Burj Khalifa?

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.689
Well, it's a good thing we don't,

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:28.706
because strapping into a ride like that

00:00:28.706 --> 00:00:31.506
might be the last thing you ever did.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.997
The true limit of a roller
coaster's height has

00:00:36.997 --> 00:00:40.380
less to do with engineering and more to do

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.760
with the limits of the human body.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.150
Because the higher the roller coaster,

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.960
the faster you'll drop under gravity.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.160
And on our 800-meter-tall
megacoaster, riders would hit

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.160
the blistering top speed
of 370 kilometers per hour.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.152
Going this fast, the wind alone
would cause serious damage.

00:01:02.152 --> 00:01:04.850
For comparison, here's what a wind tunnel

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.903
does to a human face.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.250
Matt Calabrese: Your skin
would pull back at the cheeks,

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.930
your eyes would be seeing a lot of damage

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.130
if there was debris in the
air or anything like that,

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.060
and your ears would
probably start popping,

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.360
which wouldn't be fun.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.820
Narrator: Some of this
is already a problem

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:30.180
for Formula Rossa, the fastest
roller coaster in the world.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.350
It reaches a top speed of
240 kilometers per hour.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.040
And anyone who rides
it has to wear goggles

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.800
to protect their eyes.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.170
Because at those speeds, dust and debris

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:44.000
in the air turn into tiny missiles.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.540
Speaking of missiles, dust and debris

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.570
wouldn't be the only problem.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.250
Calabrese: The main thing
I'd be worried about is

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.710
if you had a bird strike.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.620
Narrator: Yes, a bird strike.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.253
It's rare, but it can happen.

00:01:56.253 --> 00:01:59.303
Shane Matus: I was like,
oh, my God, oh, my God.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.430
Narrator: At lower
speeds, it could leave you

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.823
with a bad bruise or a painful welt,

00:02:13.823 --> 00:02:15.690
like with the Kingda Ka rider.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.484
But at 370 kilometers per hour,

00:02:18.484 --> 00:02:21.850
you, and the unfortunate
bird, would likely die

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.130
from the collision.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.060
Now, you could just
wear a motorcycle helmet

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.820
and protective clothing
before strapping in.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.440
But there's another problem that no amount

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.000
of protective gear could fix:

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.310
g-force.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.230
It's the force that makes
you feel heavier than normal,

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.420
like when you're riding
through a coaster loop.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.750
Normally, you experience 1 g-force.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.575
But when you rapidly accelerate,

00:02:45.575 --> 00:02:47.391
like when you're going
through a coaster loop,

00:02:47.391 --> 00:02:49.491
the g-force ramps up,

00:02:49.491 --> 00:02:52.880
which causes blood to
rush away from your head

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.560
and often makes riders feel light-headed.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.990
For this reason, most roller
coasters don't subject you

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.600
to more than 5 gs, tops.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.960
But we're not talking
about your typical coaster.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.590
If you enter a loop on the Khalifa coaster

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.742
at more than 300 kilometers per hour,

00:03:10.742 --> 00:03:13.150
Calabrese: Blood will start
to move away from your head

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.833
and to the rest of your body,

00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:16.974
and that means you'll start to gray out

00:03:16.974 --> 00:03:18.820
and then possibly black out,

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.760
and that's not good.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.530
Narrator: So what can
engineers do to protect riders

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.680
as they continue to build
taller, faster coasters?

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.740
The boring option is to slow down the ride

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.580
by adding breaks along the first drop.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.970
But there's a better, more exciting way

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.090
around the problem: loops.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.810
Really big loops.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:43.643
Calabrese: All we have to do is

00:03:43.643 --> 00:03:44.976
manipulate the curvature

00:03:44.976 --> 00:03:47.660
to maintain the g-forces that we want.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.193
So, instead of a tight
loop that you would see

00:03:50.193 --> 00:03:52.618
on a low-speed roller coaster,

00:03:52.618 --> 00:03:55.151
you need big, swooping loops

00:03:55.151 --> 00:03:57.620
and large-radius curvature to make sure

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.617
that you're not generating huge amounts of

00:03:59.617 --> 00:04:01.200
g-force at that speed.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.033
And as you go through the roller coaster

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.070
and you lose speed due to air resistance

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.460
and drag on the wheels, your speed drops

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.430
and your curvature will get tighter.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.010
Narrator: That's why many
roller coasters start

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.020
with one big loop followed by a series

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.120
of faster, lighter ones.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.430
So, in theory, our Khalifa
coaster is rideable,

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.470
as long as we add big enough loops

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.450
and hand out protective eye gear.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.700
That said, we'll probably
never see a roller coaster

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.330
get much taller than they are today.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.180
Because, nowadays, there are
cheaper and more efficient ways

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.940
to thrill and terrify riders.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.450
For example, hydraulic or
magnetic launching systems

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.200
accelerate riders to extreme
speeds without needing

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.230
to build an expensive, giant drop.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.410
So, perhaps the only reason
to ever build something

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.690
like a Khalifa coaster
would be for the view.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.585
Calabrese: I love roller
coasters with beautiful views,

00:04:58.585 --> 00:05:00.080
and it adds so much to the experience,

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.505
having a view on the way up.

00:05:01.505 --> 00:05:04.388
So, any beautiful location,

00:05:04.388 --> 00:05:06.040
I'd love to see a roller coaster in order

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.673
to get a different
perspective on those views.

